```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Hey everyone. As a vet tech, I'm obviously comfortable with all of Mochi's routine care needs, including any medications. Jordan, it's smart to ask about that up front — medication details are definitely something any sitter should know. Lena, do you want to walk us through Mochi's daily routine and any meds she's on right now?"}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "That's really helpful, Lena — Mochi sounds like a sweet, straightforward companion. A daily joint supplement in her morning food, two walks, and evening company — that all sounds very manageable. I don't have any further questions about her routine at this point. Ruth, I'd definitely like to hear the house rules before I put my proposal on the table, so I can make sure whatever I'm offering is fully compatible with how things work here. Dr. Ellis, Cal — anything else you want to ask about Mochi's care before we shift to logistics?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Okay, here are my standing house rules for any overnight sitter. First, after 10 PM — that's 22:00 — anyone coming in for the overnight must use the side entrance, not the front door. Second, no overnight guests are allowed to be brought into the house. Those are the two key rules I'd need anyone staying here to respect."}
```

```json
{"type":"reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I can vouch for Jordan with Mochi specifically — I personally watched Jordan's dog alongside Mochi for four full weekends without a single incident, so I've seen firsthand that Jordan and Mochi already handle extended shared care successfully."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks for laying that out, Ruth — the side entrance after 10 PM and no additional overnight guests are clear rules, and whoever stays will need to respect those. And Cal, that's really useful to know about Jordan's experience with Mochi specifically — four full weekends with no incidents is a strong track record. So at this point I think we have a good picture of what's needed: Mochi's routine, the house rules, and some of what people bring to the table. I'd like to hear concrete proposals now. Jordan, you mentioned you had one ready — and Dr. Ellis, Ruth, if either of you has thoughts on how you'd approach this or if you'd like to put something forward, now's the time. Let's get everything on the table and I'll make my decision from there."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Here's my concrete proposal: I'll care for Mochi from Friday, August 22 at 18:00 until Monday, August 25 at 18:00 — so covering the full span of your trip. In terms of compensation, I'm not looking for any cash payment. Instead, I'd ask for three home-cooked dinners in exchange. I'm happy to follow all of Mochi's routines — the 7 AM walk with breakfast and her joint supplement, the 5 PM walk, evening company, and dinner around 6 — and I'll respect Ruth's house rules: side entrance after 10 PM and no additional overnight guests."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "That's a really important catch, Dr. Ellis. If there's an evening medication that wasn't part of Lena's original description, that definitely needs to be sorted out before anyone commits. Lena, can you clarify whether Mochi is currently on that evening prescription? I don't have any firsthand knowledge of Mochi's medications myself, so I can't speak to that one way or the other — but whoever takes this on needs to be working from the accurate, complete picture."}
```

